<spell-page "kitchen sink" notebook>
	<header level="1">
		Kitchen Sink
		<header>Every component family's main example on one page, live: pick a theme and see it everywhere at once.</>
	</>

	<!-- A snapshot of the docs site's kitchen sink (`yarn site:kitchen`, each family's main example). -->
	<markdown>
		Every component family's main example, live, on one page: pick a theme and a colour scheme below and see it on
		everything at once. The choice is remembered on every page of this site. Each family's own page has the rest of
		its examples; the [theming page](/theming) says which themes restyle which components.
	</>
	<sticky class="site-sticky-bar">
		<segment appearance="secondary">
			<theme-menu/>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Elements">
		<section label="Button" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Button" description="A button indicates a possible user action. \[Button page](/button)">
				<button>Follow</button>
			</example>
			<example "Button" description="Emphasis">
				<button color="primary">Save</button>
				<button color="secondary">Okay</button>
				<button>Cancel</button>
			</example>
			<example "Button" description="Animated">
				<button reveal="slide" icon="arrow-right">Next</button>
				<button reveal="vertical" icon="cart-shopping">Shop</button>
				<button reveal="fade"><text slot="icon">$12.99 a month</text>Sign-up for a Pro account</button>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Container" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Container" description="A container limits content to a maximum width. \[Container page](/container)">
				<container>
					<text paragraph>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetuer adipiscing elit. Aenean commodo ligula eget dolor. Aenean massa strong. Cum sociis natoque penatibus et magnis dis parturient montes, nascetur ridiculus mus.</text>
					<text paragraph>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetuer adipiscing elit. Aenean commodo ligula eget dolor. Aenean massa strong. Cum sociis natoque penatibus et magnis dis parturient montes, nascetur ridiculus mus.</text>
				</container>
			</example>
			<example "Container" description="Text container">
				<html>
					<ui-container text>
						<h2>Header</h2>
						<ui-text paragraph>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetuer adipiscing elit. Aenean commodo ligula eget dolor. Aenean massa strong. Cum sociis natoque penatibus et magnis dis parturient montes, nascetur ridiculus mus.</ui-text>
						<ui-text paragraph>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetuer adipiscing elit. Aenean commodo ligula eget dolor. Aenean massa strong. Cum sociis natoque penatibus et magnis dis parturient montes, nascetur ridiculus mus.</ui-text>
					</ui-container>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Content parts" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Content parts" description="Headers, content, descriptions, metas and the other generic parts that cards, items, modals and messages share. \[Content parts page](/content-parts) · \[Actions page](/actions) · \[Author page](/author) · \[Avatar page](/avatar) · \[Content page](/content) · \[Date page](/date) · \[Description page](/description) · \[Detail page](/detail) · \[Extra page](/extra) · \[Meta page](/meta) · \[Summary page](/summary) · \[Title page](/title) · \[Value page](/value)">
				<header level="1">First header</header>
				<header level="2">Second header</header>
				<header level="3">Third header</header>
				<header level="4">Fourth header</header>
				<header level="5">Fifth header</header>
				<header level="6">Sixth header</header>
			</example>
			<example "Content parts" description="Content headers">
				<header size="huge">Huge header</header>
				<header size="large">Large header</header>
				<header>Plain header</header>
				<header size="medium">Medium header</header>
				<header size="small">Small header</header>
				<header size="tiny">Tiny header</header>
				<header size="mini">Mini header</header>
				<header size="massive" level="2">A sized page header</header>
			</example>
			<example "Content parts" description="Icon headers">
				<header align="center" icon level="2"><icon name="users" appearance="circular"/> Friends</header>
				<header icon level="2">
					<icon name="gear"/>
					<content>Account Settings <header sub>Manage your account settings and set e-mail preferences.</header></content>
				</header>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Divider" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Divider" description="A divider visually segments content into groups. \[Divider page](/divider)">
				<text paragraph>Doggie treats are good for all times of the year. Proven to be eaten by 99.9% of all dogs worldwide.</text>
				<divider/>
				<text paragraph>Doggie treats are good for all times of the year. Proven to be eaten by 99.9% of all dogs worldwide.</text>
			</example>
			<example "Divider" description="Vertical divider">
				<stack style="position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 4em; padding: 1em; border: 1px solid var(--ui-border-color);">
					<stack>
						<text paragraph>Doggie treats are good for all times of the year. Proven to be eaten by 99.9% of all dogs worldwide.</text>
					</stack>
					<divider direction="vertical">and</divider>
					<stack>
						<text paragraph>Doggie treats are good for all times of the year. Proven to be eaten by 99.9% of all dogs worldwide.</text>
					</stack>
				</stack>
			</example>
			<example "Divider" description="Horizontal divider">
				<stack style="text-align: center">
					<button type="button">Search</button>
					<divider direction="horizontal">Or</divider>
					<button type="button">Create new order</button>
				</stack>
				<divider direction="horizontal" icon="tag">Description</divider>
				<text paragraph>Doggie treats are good for all times of the year. Proven to be eaten by 99.9% of all dogs worldwide.</text>
				<divider direction="horizontal" icon="chart-column">Specifications</divider>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Emoji" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Emoji" description="An emoji is a glyph used to represent something else. \[Emoji page](/emoji)">
				<text paragraph>
					<emoji name="grinning_face_with_smiling_eyes"/>
					<emoji name="face_with_tears_of_joy"/>
					<emoji name="thumbs_up"/>
					<emoji name="red_heart"/>
					<emoji name="sun"/>
					<emoji name="flag_united_states"/>
					<emoji name="keycap_1"/>
					<emoji name="woman_technologist"/>
				</text>
			</example>
			<example "Emoji" description="In text">
				<text paragraph>That was <emoji name=":face_with_tears_of_joy:"/> hilarious, thanks <emoji name="thumbs_up" label="Approved"/></text>
			</example>
			<example "Emoji" description="Decorative">
				<text paragraph><emoji name="sparkles" label=""/> New features</text>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Flag" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Flag" description="A flag is used to represent a political state. \[Flag page](/flag)">
				<text paragraph>
					<flag country="fr"/>
					<flag country="us"/>
					<flag country="gb"/>
					<flag country="de"/>
					<flag country="jp"/>
					<flag country="br"/>
					<flag country="in"/>
					<flag country="za"/>
					<flag country="eu"/>
					<flag country="un"/>
				</text>
			</example>
			<example "Flag" description="Other flags">
				<text paragraph>
					<flag country="pride"/>
					<flag country="transgender"/>
					<flag country="pirate"/>
					<flag country="england"/>
					<flag country="scotland"/>
					<flag country="wales"/>
				</text>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Icon" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Icon" description="An icon is a glyph used to represent something else. \[Icon page](/icon)">
				<icon name="house"/>
				<icon name="users"/>
				<icon name="cloud"/>
				<icon name="puzzle-piece"/>
				<icon name="heart"/>
			</example>
			<example "Icon" description="Regular (outline)">
				<icon name="heart outline"/>
				<icon name="bell outline"/>
				<icon name="envelope outline"/>
				<icon name="circle outline"/>
			</example>
			<example "Icon" description="Brands">
				<icon name="github"/>
				<icon name="discord"/>
				<icon name="medium"/>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Image" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Image" description="An image is a graphic representation of something. \[Image page](/image)">
				<image src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22480%22 height=%22320%22 viewBox=%220 0 30 20%22%3E%3Crect width=%2230%22 height=%2220%22 fill=%22%23cbd5e1%22/%3E%3Cpath d=%22M3 17l7-8 5 6 4-4 8 6z%22 fill=%22%2394a3b8%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%2222%22 cy=%226%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%2394a3b8%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt=""/>
			</example>
			<example "Image" description="Image link">
				<image link="#image-link" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22480%22 height=%22320%22 viewBox=%220 0 30 20%22%3E%3Crect width=%2230%22 height=%2220%22 fill=%22%23cbd5e1%22/%3E%3Cpath d=%22M3 17l7-8 5 6 4-4 8 6z%22 fill=%22%2394a3b8%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%2222%22 cy=%226%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%2394a3b8%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E" alt="A landscape"/>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Input" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Input" description="An input is a field used to elicit a response from a user. \[Input page](/input) · \[Textarea page](/textarea)">
				<input placeholder="Search..." aria-label="Search"/>
			</example>
			<example "Input" description="Native types">
				<stack class="ui-cluster">
					<input type="password" placeholder="Password" aria-label="Password"/>
					<input type="email" placeholder="E-mail" aria-label="E-mail"/>
					<input type="number" placeholder="Quantity" aria-label="Quantity"/>
					<input type="date" aria-label="Date"/>
				</stack>
			</example>
			<example "Input" description="Textarea">
				<textarea fluid rows="3" placeholder="Tell us more" aria-label="Tell us more"/>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Label" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Label" description="A label displays content classification. \[Label page](/label)">
				<label icon="envelope">23</label>
				<text paragraph><html><kbd><ui-label>Ctrl</ui-label></kbd> + <kbd><ui-label>Alt</ui-label></kbd> + <kbd><ui-label>Del</ui-label></kbd> <kbd><ui-label appearance="basic">W</ui-label></kbd><kbd><ui-label appearance="basic">A</ui-label></kbd><kbd><ui-label appearance="basic">S</ui-label></kbd></html></text>
			</example>
			<example "Label" description="Image">
				<label link="#joe" image="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%2394a3b8%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23e2e8f0%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E">Joe</label>
				<label link="#elliot" image="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%2394a3b8%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23e2e8f0%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E">Elliot</label>
				<label link="#veronika" color="blue" image="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%2394a3b8%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23e2e8f0%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E" detail="Friend">Veronika</label>
				<label image="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%2394a3b8%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23e2e8f0%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E" removable>Zoe</label>
			</example>
			<example "Label" description="Pointing">
				<html>
					<ui-stack class="ui-stack">
						<ui-stack>
							<input type="text" placeholder="First name" aria-label="First name" />
							<br />
							<ui-label pointing>Please enter a value</ui-label>
						</ui-stack>
						<ui-stack>
							<ui-label pointing="below">Please enter a value</ui-label>
							<br />
							<input type="text" aria-label="Value" />
						</ui-stack>
						<ui-stack>
							<input type="text" placeholder="Username" aria-label="Username" />
							<ui-label pointing="left">That name is taken!</ui-label>
						</ui-stack>
						<ui-stack>
							<ui-label pointing="right">Your password must be 6 characters or more</ui-label>
							<input type="password" aria-label="Password" />
						</ui-stack>
						<ui-stack>
							<input type="text" aria-label="Name" />
							<ui-label color="red" pointing="left" appearance="basic">That name is taken!</ui-label>
						</ui-stack>
					</ui-stack>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="List" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "List" description="A list is used to group related content. \[List page](/list)">
				<list>
					<item>Apples</item>
					<item>Pears</item>
					<item>Oranges</item>
				</list>
			</example>
			<example "List" description="Icons">
				<list>
					<item icon="users">
						<content>Fomantic UI</content>
					</item>
					<item icon="location dot">
						<content>Worldwide</content>
					</item>
					<item icon="mail">
						<content>
							<link link="mailto:contact@example.com">contact@example.com</link>
						</content>
					</item>
					<item icon="linkify">
						<content>
							<link link="#site">example.com</link>
						</content>
					</item>
				</list>
			</example>
			<example "List" description="Relaxed, divided, with headers">
				<list spacing="lg" divided>
					<item icon="github">
						<content>
							<header link="#ui">fomantic/Fomantic-UI</header>
							<description>Updated 10 mins ago</description>
						</content>
					</item>
					<item icon="github">
						<content>
							<header link="#docs">fomantic/Fomantic-UI-Docs</header>
							<description>Updated 22 mins ago</description>
						</content>
					</item>
					<item icon="github">
						<content>
							<header link="#less">fomantic/Fomantic-UI-LESS</header>
							<description>Updated 34 mins ago</description>
						</content>
					</item>
				</list>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Loader" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Loader" description="A loader alerts a user to wait for an activity to complete. \[Loader page](/loader)">
				<stack style="position: relative; height: 8em; border: 1px solid var(--ui-border-color); border-radius: var(--ui-radius)">
					<loader visible/>
				</stack>
			</example>
			<example "Loader" description="Text loader">
				<stack style="position: relative; height: 8em; border: 1px solid var(--ui-border-color); border-radius: var(--ui-radius)">
					<loader visible text>Loading</loader>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Placeholder" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Placeholder" description="A placeholder is used to reserve space for content that soon will appear in a layout. \[Placeholder page](/placeholder)">
				<placeholder>
					<placeholder-header image>
						<placeholder-line/>
						<placeholder-line/>
					</placeholder-header>
					<placeholder-paragraph>
						<placeholder-line length="medium"/>
						<placeholder-line length="short"/>
					</placeholder-paragraph>
				</placeholder>
			</example>
			<example "Placeholder" description="Cards">
				<stack style="--min-column-size: 12em" class="ui-grid">
					<stack style="padding: 1em; border: 1px solid var(--ui-border-color); border-radius: var(--ui-radius)">
						<placeholder fluid>
							<placeholder-image rectangular/>
							<placeholder-header>
								<placeholder-line length="very short"/>
								<placeholder-line length="medium"/>
							</placeholder-header>
							<placeholder-paragraph>
								<placeholder-line length="short"/>
							</placeholder-paragraph>
						</placeholder>
					</stack>
					<stack style="padding: 1em; border: 1px solid var(--ui-border-color); border-radius: var(--ui-radius)">
						<placeholder fluid>
							<placeholder-image rectangular/>
							<placeholder-header>
								<placeholder-line length="very short"/>
								<placeholder-line length="medium"/>
							</placeholder-header>
							<placeholder-paragraph>
								<placeholder-line length="short"/>
							</placeholder-paragraph>
						</placeholder>
					</stack>
					<stack style="padding: 1em; border: 1px solid var(--ui-border-color); border-radius: var(--ui-radius)">
						<placeholder fluid>
							<placeholder-image rectangular/>
							<placeholder-header>
								<placeholder-line length="very short"/>
								<placeholder-line length="medium"/>
							</placeholder-header>
							<placeholder-paragraph>
								<placeholder-line length="short"/>
							</placeholder-paragraph>
						</placeholder>
					</stack>
				</stack>
			</example>
			<example "Placeholder" description="Consecutive placeholders">
				<stack>
					<placeholder>
						<placeholder-header image>
							<placeholder-line/>
							<placeholder-line/>
						</placeholder-header>
					</placeholder>
					<placeholder>
						<placeholder-header image>
							<placeholder-line/>
							<placeholder-line/>
						</placeholder-header>
					</placeholder>
					<placeholder>
						<placeholder-header image>
							<placeholder-line/>
							<placeholder-line/>
						</placeholder-header>
					</placeholder>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Rail" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Rail" description="A rail is used to show accompanying content outside the boundaries of the main view of a site. \[Rail page](/rail)">
				<stack style="margin-inline: 20em">
					<segment>
						<rail position="left">
							<segment>Left rail content</segment>
						</rail>
						<rail position="right">
							<segment>Right rail content</segment>
						</rail>
						<text paragraph>Main content. Te eum doming eirmod, nominati pertinacia argumentum ad his.</text>
					</segment>
				</stack>
			</example>
			<example "Rail" description="Internal">
				<segment>
					<rail position="left" internal>
						<segment>Left rail content</segment>
					</rail>
					<rail position="right" internal>
						<segment>Right rail content</segment>
					</rail>
					<text paragraph>Main content. Te eum doming eirmod, nominati pertinacia argumentum ad his.</text>
				</segment>
			</example>
			<example "Rail" description="Dividing">
				<stack style="margin-inline: 20em">
					<segment>
						<rail position="left" dividing>
							<segment>Left rail content</segment>
						</rail>
						<rail position="right" dividing>
							<segment>Right rail content</segment>
						</rail>
						<text paragraph>Main content. Te eum doming eirmod, nominati pertinacia argumentum ad his.</text>
					</segment>
				</stack>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Reveal" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Reveal" description="A reveal displays additional content in place of previous content when activated. \[Reveal page](/reveal)">
				<reveal fade>
					<image height="150" width="150" alt="Avatar" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22150%22 height=%22150%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%2394a3b8%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23e2e8f0%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E" slot="visible"/>
					<image height="150" width="150" alt="Profile" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22150%22 height=%22150%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%230f766e%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23ccfbf1%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E" slot="hidden"/>
				</reveal>
			</example>
			<example "Reveal" description="Move">
				<reveal move>
					<image height="150" width="150" alt="Avatar" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22150%22 height=%22150%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%2394a3b8%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23e2e8f0%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E" slot="visible"/>
					<image height="150" width="150" alt="Profile" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22150%22 height=%22150%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%230f766e%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23ccfbf1%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E" slot="hidden"/>
				</reveal>
				<reveal move="right">
					<image height="150" width="150" alt="Avatar" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22150%22 height=%22150%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%2394a3b8%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23e2e8f0%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E" slot="visible"/>
					<image height="150" width="150" alt="Profile" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22150%22 height=%22150%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%230f766e%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23ccfbf1%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E" slot="hidden"/>
				</reveal>
				<reveal move="up">
					<image height="150" width="150" alt="Avatar" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22150%22 height=%22150%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%2394a3b8%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23e2e8f0%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E" slot="visible"/>
					<image height="150" width="150" alt="Profile" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22150%22 height=%22150%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%230f766e%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23ccfbf1%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E" slot="hidden"/>
				</reveal>
				<reveal move="down">
					<image height="150" width="150" alt="Avatar" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22150%22 height=%22150%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%2394a3b8%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23e2e8f0%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E" slot="visible"/>
					<image height="150" width="150" alt="Profile" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22150%22 height=%22150%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%230f766e%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23ccfbf1%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E" slot="hidden"/>
				</reveal>
			</example>
			<example "Reveal" description="Rotate">
				<reveal rotate>
					<image style="border-radius: 50%" height="150" width="150" alt="Avatar" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22150%22 height=%22150%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%2394a3b8%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23e2e8f0%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E" slot="visible"/>
					<image style="border-radius: 50%" height="150" width="150" alt="Profile" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22150%22 height=%22150%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%230f766e%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23ccfbf1%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E" slot="hidden"/>
				</reveal>
				<reveal rotate="left">
					<image style="border-radius: 50%" height="150" width="150" alt="Avatar" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22150%22 height=%22150%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%2394a3b8%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23e2e8f0%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E" slot="visible"/>
					<image style="border-radius: 50%" height="150" width="150" alt="Profile" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22 width=%22150%22 height=%22150%22 viewBox=%220 0 10 10%22%3E%3Crect width=%2210%22 height=%2210%22 fill=%22%230f766e%22/%3E%3Ccircle cx=%225%22 cy=%224%22 r=%222%22 fill=%22%23ccfbf1%22/%3E%3C/svg%3E" slot="hidden"/>
				</reveal>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Segment" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Segment" description="A segment is used to create a grouping of related content. \[Segment page](/segment)">
				<segment>
					<text paragraph>Te eum doming eirmod, nominati pertinacia argumentum ad his.</text>
				</segment>
			</example>
			<example "Segment" description="Placeholder segment">
				<segment placeholder="">
					<text style="text-align: center" paragraph>No documents are listed for this customer.</text>
					<button type="button">Add document</button>
				</segment>
			</example>
			<example "Segment" description="Raised">
				<segment appearance="raised">
					<text paragraph>Te eum doming eirmod, nominati pertinacia argumentum ad his.</text>
				</segment>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Step" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Step" description="A step shows the completion status of an activity in a series of activities. \[Step page](/step)">
				<steps>
					<step icon="truck" heading="Shipping" description="Choose your shipping options"/>
				</steps>
			</example>
			<example "Step" description="Steps">
				<steps>
					<step icon="truck" heading="Shipping" description="Choose your shipping options"/>
					<step selected icon="credit-card" heading="Billing" description="Enter billing information"/>
					<step disabled icon="circle-info" heading="Confirm Order"/>
				</steps>
			</example>
			<example "Step" description="Ordered">
				<steps ordered>
					<step completed heading="Shipping" description="Choose your shipping options"/>
					<step completed heading="Billing" description="Enter billing information"/>
					<step selected heading="Confirm Order" description="Verify order details"/>
				</steps>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Text" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Text" description="A text is used to style some inline text with a simple color. \[Text page](/text)">
				<text paragraph>This is <text color="red">red inline text</text> and <text color="blue">this is blue inline text</text> and <text color="purple">this is purple inline text</text>.</text>
				<text paragraph>
					<text color="primary">Primary</text>
					<text color="secondary">Secondary</text>
					<text color="orange">Orange</text>
					<text color="yellow">Yellow</text>
					<text color="olive">Olive</text>
					<text color="green">Green</text>
					<text color="teal">Teal</text>
					<text color="violet">Violet</text>
					<text color="pink">Pink</text>
					<text color="brown">Brown</text>
					<text color="grey">Grey</text>
					<text color="black">Black</text>
				</text>
			</example>
			<example "Text" description="Semantic colors">
				<text paragraph>This is <text state="info">info inline text</text> and <text state="success">this is success inline text</text> and <text state="warning">this is warning inline text</text> and <text state="error">this is error inline text</text>.</text>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Video" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Video" description="A video plays a video file in the browser's own player. \[Video page](/video) · \[Audio page](/audio)">
				<video src="/components/ui/examples/media/sample.webm" captions="examples/media/sample.vtt" ratio="16/9" label="A ball rolls across the screen" style="max-width: 32em"/>
			</example>
			<example "Video" description="Audio">
				<audio src="/components/ui/examples/media/chime.wav" controls label="A chime"/>
			</example>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Collections">
		<section label="Breadcrumb" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Breadcrumb" description="A breadcrumb is used to show hierarchy between content. \[Breadcrumb page](/breadcrumb)">
				<breadcrumbs aria-label="Breadcrumb demo">
					<breadcrumb link="#home">Home</breadcrumb>
					<breadcrumb link="#store">Store</breadcrumb>
					<breadcrumb selected>T-Shirt</breadcrumb>
				</breadcrumbs>
			</example>
			<example "Breadcrumb" description="Semantic list, token divider">
				<breadcrumbs aria-label="Token divider demo">
					<breadcrumb link="#home">Home</breadcrumb>
					<breadcrumb link="#store">Store</breadcrumb>
					<breadcrumb selected>T-Shirt</breadcrumb>
				</breadcrumbs>
				<breadcrumbs aria-label="Custom divider demo" divider="›">
					<breadcrumb link="#home">Home</breadcrumb>
					<breadcrumb link="#store">Store</breadcrumb>
					<breadcrumb selected>T-Shirt</breadcrumb>
				</breadcrumbs>
			</example>
			<example "Breadcrumb" description="Icon divider">
				<breadcrumbs aria-label="Icon divider demo" divider-icon="chevron right">
					<breadcrumb link="#home">Home</breadcrumb>
					<breadcrumb link="#registration">Registration</breadcrumb>
					<breadcrumb selected>Personal Information</breadcrumb>
				</breadcrumbs>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Form" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Form" description="A form displays a set of related user input fields in a structured way. \[Form page](/form)">
				<form>
					<field label="First Name">
						<input id="fm-types-first" name="first-name" placeholder="First Name"/>
					</field>
					<field label="Last Name">
						<input id="fm-types-last" name="last-name" placeholder="Last Name"/>
					</field>
					<field>
						<checkbox name="terms">I agree to the Terms and Conditions</checkbox>
					</field>
					<button type="submit">Submit</button>
				</form>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Grid" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Grid" description="A grid is used to harmonize negative space in a layout. \[Grid page](/grid)">
				<grid>
					<column width="4">
						<text paragraph>Four wide</text>
					</column>
					<column width="4">
						<text paragraph>Four wide</text>
					</column>
					<column width="4">
						<text paragraph>Four wide</text>
					</column>
					<column width="4">
						<text paragraph>Four wide</text>
					</column>
					<column width="8">
						<text paragraph>Eight wide</text>
					</column>
					<column width="8">
						<text paragraph>Eight wide</text>
					</column>
				</grid>
			</example>
			<example "Grid" description="Divided">
				<grid divided columns="3">
					<row>
						<column>
							<text paragraph>One</text>
						</column>
						<column>
							<text paragraph>Two</text>
						</column>
						<column>
							<text paragraph>Three</text>
						</column>
					</row>
					<row>
						<column>
							<text paragraph>Four</text>
						</column>
						<column>
							<text paragraph>Five</text>
						</column>
						<column>
							<text paragraph>Six</text>
						</column>
					</row>
				</grid>
			</example>
			<example "Grid" description="Vertically divided">
				<grid divided="vertically">
					<row columns="2">
						<column>
							<text paragraph>One</text>
						</column>
						<column>
							<text paragraph>Two</text>
						</column>
					</row>
					<row columns="3">
						<column>
							<text paragraph>Three</text>
						</column>
						<column>
							<text paragraph>Four</text>
						</column>
						<column>
							<text paragraph>Five</text>
						</column>
					</row>
				</grid>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Menu" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Menu" description="A menu displays grouped navigation actions. \[Menu page](/menu)">
				<menu items="3" aria-label="Menu demo">
					<item link="#editorials" selected>Editorials</item>
					<item link="#reviews">Reviews</item>
					<item link="#events">Upcoming Events</item>
				</menu>
			</example>
			<example "Menu" description="Secondary menu">
				<menu appearance="secondary" aria-label="Secondary demo">
					<item link="#home" active>Home</item>
					<item link="#messages">Messages</item>
					<item link="#friends">Friends</item>
					<menu position="right">
						<item link="#logout">Logout</item>
					</menu>
				</menu>
			</example>
			<example "Menu" description="Pointing">
				<menu appearance="pointing" aria-label="Pointing demo">
					<item link="#home">Home</item>
					<item link="#messages" selected>Messages</item>
					<item link="#friends">Friends</item>
					<menu position="right">
						<item link="#search">Search</item>
					</menu>
				</menu>
				<menu appearance="secondary pointing" aria-label="Secondary pointing demo">
					<item link="#home" selected>Home</item>
					<item link="#messages">Messages</item>
					<item link="#friends">Friends</item>
					<menu position="right">
						<item link="#logout">Logout</item>
					</menu>
				</menu>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Message" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Message" description="A message displays information that explains nearby content. \[Message page](/message)">
				<message>
					<header>Changes in Service</header>
					<text paragraph>We just updated our privacy policy here to better service our customers. We recommend reviewing the changes.</text>
				</message>
			</example>
			<example "Message" description="List message">
				<message heading="New site features">
					<list bulleted>
						<item>You can now have cover images on blog pages</item>
						<item>Drafts will now auto-save while writing</item>
					</list>
				</message>
			</example>
			<example "Message" description="Icon message">
				<message heading="Have you heard about our mailing list?">
					<icon slot="icon" name="envelope"/>
					<text paragraph>Get the best news in your e-mail every day.</text>
				</message>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Property Editor" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Property Editor" description="A property editor draws a form from a schema:  one field per property, in folding groups, for one thing or many. \[Property Editor page](/property-editor)">
				<html>
					<ui-property-editor compact show-defaults label="Routine" style="max-width: 340px" schema="{\"name\": \"Routine\", \"attributes\": \[
                    {\"name\": \"name\", \"kind\": \"string\", \"type\": \"text\", \"description\": \"\", \"hint\": \"LaTeX\", \"tip\": \"Shown on the circuit.\"},
                    {\"name\": \"kind\", \"kind\": \"enum\", \"type\": \"choice\", \"values\": \[\"gate\", \"measure\", \"reset\"], \"default\": \"gate\", \"description\": \"\"},
                    {\"name\": \"steps\", \"kind\": \"number\", \"type\": \"number\", \"default\": 1, \"description\": \"\"},
                    {\"name\": \"angle\", \"kind\": \"string\", \"type\": \"text\", \"description\": \"\", \"hint\": \"LaTeX or a #\"},
                    {\"name\": \"align\", \"kind\": \"textAlign\", \"default\": \"left\", \"description\": \"\", \"tip\": \"Where its label sits.\"},
                    {\"name\": \"color\", \"kind\": \"color\", \"description\": \"\"},
                    {\"name\": \"margin\", \"kind\": \"json\", \"type\": \"sides\", \"description\": \"\"},
                    {\"name\": \"padding\", \"kind\": \"json\", \"type\": \"sides\", \"description\": \"\"},
                    {\"name\": \"controlled\", \"kind\": \"boolean\", \"description\": \"\", \"tip\": \"Runs only when its control is on.\"},
                    {\"name\": \"inverse\", \"kind\": \"boolean\", \"description\": \"\"},
                    {\"name\": \"barrier\", \"kind\": \"boolean\", \"description\": \"\"},
                    {\"name\": \"visible\", \"kind\": \"boolean\", \"default\": true, \"description\": \"\"},
                    {\"name\": \"locked\", \"kind\": \"boolean\", \"description\": \"\"}
                  ]}" value="{\"name\": \"QFT\", \"kind\": \"gate\", \"steps\": 3, \"angle\": \"\", \"align\": \"center\", \"color\": \"violet\", \"margin\": \"0 0 0 0\", \"padding\": \"4 8 4 8\", \"controlled\": true, \"inverse\": false, \"barrier\": true, \"visible\": true, \"locked\": false}">
						<ui-property-group label="Defaults" collapsible>
							<ui-property name="name"></ui-property>
							<ui-property name="kind"></ui-property>
							<ui-property name="steps"></ui-property>
							<ui-property name="angle"></ui-property>
						</ui-property-group>
						<ui-property-group label="Appearance" collapsible>
							<ui-property name="align"></ui-property>
							<ui-property name="color"></ui-property>
							<ui-property name="margin"></ui-property>
							<ui-property name="padding"></ui-property>
						</ui-property-group>
						<ui-property-group label="Behaviour" collapsible>
							<ui-property name="controlled"></ui-property>
							<ui-property name="inverse"></ui-property>
							<ui-property name="barrier"></ui-property>
						</ui-property-group>
						<ui-property-group label="Layout" collapsible>
							<ui-property name="visible"></ui-property>
							<ui-property name="locked"></ui-property>
						</ui-property-group>
					</ui-property-editor>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Table" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Table" description="A table displays a collection of data grouped into rows. \[Table page](/table)">
				<table celled>
					<row header>
						<cell>Name</cell>
						<cell>Status</cell>
						<cell>Notes</cell>
					</row>
					<row>
						<cell>John</cell>
						<cell>Approved</cell>
						<cell>None</cell>
					</row>
					<row>
						<cell>Jamie</cell>
						<cell>Approved</cell>
						<cell>Requires call</cell>
					</row>
					<row>
						<cell>Jill</cell>
						<cell>Denied</cell>
						<cell>None</cell>
					</row>
					<row footer>
						<cell header>3 People</cell>
						<cell header>2 Approved</cell>
						<cell/>
					</row>
				</table>
			</example>
			<example "Table" description="Definition">
				<table definition celled>
					<row header>
						<cell/>
						<cell>Arguments</cell>
						<cell>Description</cell>
					</row>
					<row>
						<cell>reset rating</cell>
						<cell>None</cell>
						<cell>Resets rating to default value</cell>
					</row>
					<row>
						<cell>set rating</cell>
						<cell>rating (integer)</cell>
						<cell>Sets the current star rating to specified value</cell>
					</row>
				</table>
			</example>
			<example "Table" description="Structured">
				<html>
					<ui-table appearance="structured" celled>
						<table>
							<thead>
								<tr>
									<th rowspan="2" scope="col">Name</th>
									<th rowspan="2" scope="col">Type</th>
									<th rowspan="2" scope="col">Files</th>
									<th colspan="3" scope="colgroup">Languages</th>
								</tr>
								<tr>
									<th scope="col">Ruby</th>
									<th scope="col">JavaScript</th>
									<th scope="col">Python</th>
								</tr>
							</thead>
							<tbody>
								<tr>
									<td>Alpha Team</td>
									<td>Project 1</td>
									<td class="right aligned">2</td>
									<td class="center aligned">Yes</td>
									<td></td>
									<td></td>
								</tr>
								<tr>
									<td rowspan="2">Beta Team</td>
									<td>Project 1</td>
									<td class="right aligned">52</td>
									<td class="center aligned">Yes</td>
									<td></td>
									<td></td>
								</tr>
								<tr>
									<td>Project 2</td>
									<td class="right aligned">12</td>
									<td></td>
									<td class="center aligned">Yes</td>
									<td></td>
								</tr>
							</tbody>
						</table>
					</ui-table>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Terms" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing>
			<example "Terms" description="Terms list facts as a label and a value each, lined up. \[Terms page](/terms)">
				<terms>
					<term label="Suit" value="hearts"/>
					<term label="Rank" value="queen"/>
					<term label="Played by">
						<label color="blue">Jamie</label>
					</term>
				</terms>
			</example>
			<example "Terms" description="Horizontal">
